 "tier1Summary": "Washington opened a new tariff front: [[p:Office of the United States Trade Representative|USTR]] proposed [[e:Section 301 of the Trade Act of 1974|Section 301]] duties of 15–35% on 14 economies, from the EU and Japan to China and Vietnam, plus a 10% tariff on Brazilian aircraft. Canada and Mexico were spared while their own talks drag on. Commerce also shut Chinese firms' cloud access to advanced AI chips, and a jury convicted [[p:Huawei]].\n\nBrazil passed Lula's fiscal adjustment; Argentina's risk premium jumped after a technical recession; Venezuelan police blocked a wage march on Miraflores.\n\nElsewhere, Saudi Arabia says it downed Houthi missiles aimed at Riyadh, Iran claims mines and drone kills in Hormuz, and EU leaders began haggling over the 2028–34 budget.",
